Title: THE GARDEN HAS A GHOST
Credit: Mochiichao Show EP01 - script v1 (REVISED per Jamar 2026-10-27)

= VOICE CONVENTION: Creatures do NOT speak words. They vocalize -
= cries and sounds (their repo cry files). DECIDED (Jamar,
= 2026-10-27): pure cries and sounds only - no name-saying.
= Only Mochiko has word-lines.
= Creature "lines" below are vocalization + performance notes.

EXT. GARDEN GATE - MORNING

A wooden gate. A new sign: GARDEN KEEPER. MOCHIKO (12) arrives with a backpack bigger than she is. The gate swings open BY ITSELF -- because MOCHII is bouncing on it, chirping a fast, excited bouncing cry.

MOCHIKO
Okay. First rule of the garden: the gate is a trampoline. Got it.

Mochii bounces in circles around her, pure joy, cry going like a squeaky metronome.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
And you're the welcoming committee.

DOROWANI steps in, carrying a thick MANUAL almost as tall as Mochii. He sets it down in front of Mochiko and taps the cover, twice, like a gavel. A low, steady croak.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
(reading the cover)
"Garden Manual." ...You want me to read rule one?

Dorowani nods, huge and solemn. Mochii nods so fast it blurs.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
(reading)
"Rule one: mind the gate." Huh. That-- okay, that IS just the gate one.

A deep, patient sigh-croak from Dorowani: told-you-so.

INT. GARDEN POND - CONTINUOUS

Mochii stacks berries into a pyramid, humming squeaks at each one. Behind them, unseen, the pyramid UN-stacks itself, one berry at a time.

MOCHIKO
--and these are the good berries, and nobody touches the good berries, and--

Mochii turns. Stares at the un-stacked berries. One long, baffled squeak.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
You stacked those. Who unstacked those?

A wooden toy DUCK rolls past. UPHILL. Both of them watch it go.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
Ducks don't roll uphill.

KITTEMBER's flame ORB flickers hard at the empty air. Kittember freezes mid-lick, ears flat, a thin surprised mewl.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
Something cold just walked past you, didn't it.

EXT. GARDEN GREEN - DAY

GABU stomps in wearing a fishing net like a cape and beats his chest once -- a big, foghorn bellow of confidence.

MOCHIKO
You want to catch it.

Bigger bellow. He points at himself. At the pond. At himself.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
By supper. Sure. Why not.

SPROUTLE is on the ground, cheek near the grass, looking at a trail of little FROST PATCHES. A soft, dawning chirp -- then an urgent one, tugging Mochiko's sleeve with a leaf.

MOCHIKO
They're not random. It's a path. Sproutle... it's pointing at the pond. It's GIVING us directions?

EXT. GARDEN POND - DUSK

Five keepers behind a bush. The frost trail ends at the water. Gabu LUNGES -- splashes -- comes up holding pure SMOKE, which pours through his fingers. A wet, deflated honk.

MOCHIKO
Caught it. Not caught it.

Kittember's orb FLARES. A huge shadow rises on the mist -- tall, spiky -- Sproutle squeaks an apology at full volume and flattens.

MOCHIKO
That's Sproutle's shadow. THAT'S just Sproutle's shadow. Everybody breathe.

The mist parts. Small. Dark. Shaking. WISPKIN -- the garden's night keeper -- holding the toy duck up like an apology. The softest sound yet: a wisp of a wail, up at the end like a question.

MOCHIKO
...Hi. You kept the garden all night, didn't you. Every night.

Wispkin's smoke curls down, shy.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
You moved my-- HER berries so somebody would follow you. You just wanted to be introduced properly.

A tiny nod. The wail again, warmer.

MOCHIKO (CONT'D)
Then let's do it properly.

EXT. GARDEN GATE - NIGHT

The keeper board by the gate. Mochiko paints the new name in, careful and fresh: WISPKIN - NIGHT KEEPER.

MOCHIKO
(reading from the manual)
"Rule twelve: Everything in the garden belongs to somebody... And everybody belongs to the Garden."

She looks at the board. At all six of them. Nobody says anything else. The crickets do it for them.

Mochii's cry goes off like a firework. Gabu bellows. Wispkin floats UP for the first time, smoke swirling, and rings the gate bell with its tail of smoke.

TAG - Gabu still wearing the net. As a hat. He tips it, grandly.

MOCHIKO
It's a successful hat, Gabu. It's a successful hat.

STINGER - EXT. THE DARK FOREST - DAY

Past the garden gate, where the path gives up. A forest in FULL DAYLIGHT that the light doesn't reach into. The sun is up. The forest floor is in night anyway.

No music. Birdsong from the garden side -- and none from in there. The trees are too still for the breeze we can hear.

Something far in the dark between the trunks stops moving. We never see what it is. We only see it stop.

SUBTITLE burns in, low on the frame, and holds:

= "Everything in the garden belongs to somebody... And everybody belongs to the Garden."

Hold. Hold. One leaf falls, straight down, in no wind at all.

SMASH TO BLACK.

= END OF EP01 =
